      "content": "HTML Tags and Elements"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "An HTML tag provides information to the browser on how to structure the content."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "For example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "The <p> tag informs the browser that the content is a paragraph.",
        "Similarly, the <h1> tag is used to define a heading."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Opening and Closing Tags"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "HTML tags often come in pairs and are enclosed by angle brackets <>. In the code below,"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "<h1> indicates the start of a heading 1, and </h1> indicates the end.",
        "<p> indicates the start of a paragraph, and </p> indicates the end."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<h1>This is a Heading</h1>\n2<p>This is a paragraph.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Run this code and see the output for yourself."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Once you use a tag with proper syntax, it becomes an HTML element."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "So, the code you ran above is tags turned into elements that the browser understands. For example:"
